   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the Good Seed Church of God, Inc. to file an application for exemption from real property taxes for a certain parcel of land located in the hamlet of Islip Terrace",
    "basePrintNo": "S6738",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6738-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6738\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to authorize the Good Seed Church of God, Inc. to file an\napplication for exemption from real property taxes for a certain\nparcel of land located in the hamlet of Islip Terrace\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA :\n\nTo authorize the assessor of the Town of Islip to accept from Good\nSeed Church of God, Inc. an application for exemption from real\nproperty taxes for the 2014-2015 assessment role.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of this bill authorizes the Town of Islip, county of\nSuffolk, to accept from the Good Seed Church of God, Inc., a\nnot-for-profit organization, an application for an exemption of real\nproperty taxes for the parcel located at 196 Seacliff Street in the\nhamlet of Islip Terrace in the Town of Islip, county of Suffolk. If\nsatisfied that such not-for-profit organization acquired the title to\nthe property for which it seeks exemption subsequent to the taxable\nstatus date establish for such roll and prior to the taxable status\ndate for the next ensuing assessment roll, the assessor of the town of\nIslip may grant exemption from all taxation beginning with the date of\nacquisition of the property by such not-for-profit organization and\nmake appropriate correction to the subject roll. If exemption is\ngranted, the governing body or tax department may provide for the\nrefund of those taxes paid, and cancel taxes, fines, penalties or\ninterest remaining unpaid.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nExisting law authorizes tax exemptions to be granted after the taxable\nstatus date has passed if a bill is chaptered authorizing an assessor\nto accept a late application.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
